{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@5/schema.json",
  "workspaces": {
    ".": {
      "entry": [
        "caido.config.ts",
        "packages/caido.config.ts",
        "scripts/ci/*.mjs",
        "scripts/ci/**/*.spec.ts",
        "scripts/spike/*.mjs",
        "tests/**/*.spec.ts",
        "tier1/*/src/index.ts"
      ],
      "project": [
        "scripts/ci/**/*.{ts,mjs}",
        "scripts/spike/**/*.mjs",
        "tests/**/*.ts",
        "tier1/*/src/**/*.ts",
        "*.{ts,js}"
      ]
    },
    "packages/engine": {
      "project": ["src/**/*.ts"],
      "entry": ["src/**/*.spec.ts"]
    },
    "packages/backend": {
      "entry": ["src/index.ts", "src/**/*.spec.ts"],
      "project": ["src/**/*.ts"],
      "ignoreDependencies": [
        // `@caido/sdk-backend` IS NO LONGER LISTED HERE. It was, carrying the
        // note that "no source imports it yet" and that `sdk: any` at the
        // boundary was the honest annotation until the RPC surface justified a
        // type. Plan 05-07 landed that justification: `src/api/spec.ts` declares
        // the plugin package specification and `init()` takes a
        // spec-typed parameter, so the package is reached through the backend
        // tsconfig's `types` list and knip resolves it. Removed rather than left
        // as a harmless no-op, for the same reason the frontend's
        // `@defminer/engine` entry was: an ignore that has stopped being needed
        // is an ignore that starts hiding the next real one.
        //
        // Provided BY THE RUNTIME, never installed. `sqlite` is one of the ten
        // specifiers the Phase 0 capability probe loaded successfully inside
        // Caido 0.57.1, it is externalised by the build, and it is typed by
        // @caido/quickjs-types. See scripts/ci/check-bundle-imports.mjs.
        "sqlite",
        // Same category as `sqlite`, and reached the same way. `caido:plugin` is
        // an ambient module declared by @caido/sdk-backend's typing.d.ts, not a
        // package on disk; `api/spec.ts` imports `APISDK` from it as a TYPE, so
        // nothing is emitted and the shipped bundle's import set is unchanged
        // (scripts/ci/check-bundle-imports.mjs reads the built artifact, which
        // is the only place that question can be answered honestly).
        "caido"
      ]
    },
    "packages/frontend": {
      // `src/index.ts` is the plugin entry Caido calls. The vite / tailwind /
      // postcss configs are NOT listed: knip already treats them as entries by
      // default and naming them again is a redundant pattern it reports.
      "entry": ["src/index.ts", "src/**/*.spec.ts", "externals.mjs"],
      // `@defminer/engine` IS NO LONGER LISTED BELOW. It was, carrying the
      // note "Remove this entry when the first import lands", and plan 05-05
      // landed it: src/safety/display.ts imports forDisplay, forEvidence,
      // TABLE_CELL_MAX_GRAPHEMES and EVIDENCE_PANEL_MAX_GRAPHEMES from
      // @defminer/engine/sanitise. Removed rather than left in place as a
      // harmless no-op, because an ignore that has stopped being needed is an
      // ignore that starts hiding the next real one.
      // `@vueuse/core` IS NO LONGER LISTED BELOW. It was, carrying the note
      // "Remove when 05-07 and 05-08 import them", and plan 05-08 landed the
      // import: src/stores/coalescer.ts composes useDebounceFn and
      // useThrottleFn to hold 05-UI-SPEC.md's 500 ms window and its two
      // reactions per second. Removed rather than left as a harmless no-op,
      // for the same reason the `@defminer/engine` entry was: an ignore that
      // has stopped being needed is an ignore that starts hiding the next real
      // one — and knip reports the stale entry itself as a configuration hint,
      // so leaving it costs a line of permanent noise beside a real finding.
      // `ignoreDependencies` IS GONE from this workspace as of plan 05-09.
      // Its last entry was `vue-virtual-scroller`, carrying the note "Remove
      // when the table imports it" — and 05-09's InventoryTable.vue imports
      // `RecycleScroller` from it. Removed rather than left as a harmless
      // no-op, for the same reason the `@defminer/engine` and `@vueuse/core`
      // entries above were: an ignore that has stopped being needed is an
      // ignore that starts hiding the next real one, and knip reports the
      // stale entry itself as a configuration hint.
      //
      // AND `@jridgewell/sourcemap-codec` IS NO LONGER LISTED EITHER. Plan
      // 07-03 added it back for exactly one wave, carrying the note "REMOVE
      // THIS ENTRY WHEN 07-08's VIEWER IMPORTS THE CODEC, in the same edit" —
      // because D-16 relocates the codec into this workspace so the VLQ decode
      // runs in the operator's browser rather than on the proxy thread, and the
      // DECLARATION had to land a wave before the IMPORT so that
      // packages/backend/src/codec-prohibition.spec.ts (the D-17 capability
      // ban) could say where the codec legitimately lives.
      //
      // Plan 07-08 landed the import: src/components/SourcePositionStrip.vue
      // imports `decode` from it, and that component's spec asserts by an
      // exact-set walk of the frontend source tree that it is the ONLY consumer
      // — which is the property the whole relocation exists to establish.
      // Removed in the same edit, as promised, and for the same reason the
      // three notes above were: an ignore that has stopped being needed is an
      // ignore that starts hiding the next real one.
      //
      // The root devDependency is NOT removed and must not be:
      // tier1/parse/src/index.ts is the SPIKE-06 probe and knip treats
      // `tier1/*/src/index.ts` as a root-workspace entry point, so removing it
      // would make the probe unbuildable.
      "project": ["src/**/*.{ts,vue}", "*.{ts,mjs,cjs}"]
    }
  },
  // RESTORED TO `error` BY PLAN 01-03, as plan 01-02 asked for in this file.
  //
  // knip is here first for the DET-03 boundary, and that part was always ERROR:
  // packages/engine declares NO dependencies at all, so an engine module that
  // reaches for the backend or for any @caido/* package is reported as an
  // unlisted dependency and fails the gate.
  //
  // 01-02 set `exports` and `types` to `warn` because plan 01-01 had deliberately
  // shipped reachable-but-unconsumed seams, and reporting them as errors would
  // have meant either deleting seams that were already spoken for or silencing
  // the check entirely. It left a note addressed to this plan. Restoring them
  // matters because `warn` is not a gate: a genuinely dead export added tomorrow
  // would print alongside the twenty-six expected ones and change nothing.
  //
  // WHAT IT COST, STATED RATHER THAN BURIED. Two things were needed, and the
  // first is a real weakening:
  //
  //   `ignoreExportsUsedInFile: true` — knip otherwise reports every type that is
  //   exported but only referenced inside its own module, which in this codebase
  //   is sixteen of them (AdmitSdk, PassiveDeps, ArtifactRow, MigrationReport and
  //   so on — types declared next to the function that takes them). THE HOLE: a
  //   genuinely dead export that happens to be referenced once in its own file is
  //   now invisible. That is a smaller hole than `warn`, which hides everything,
  //   but it is not nothing and should be revisited when the frontend in Phase 5
  //   gives most of these types a cross-module consumer.
  //
  //   CLOSED BY PLAN 05-01 — `false`, see below. The note above named the exact
  //   condition for closing it and Phase 5 met it.
  //
  //   One `@public` JSDoc tag, on store/db.ts's `resetDbHandle` — the single
  //   remaining export with no consumer, named for plan 01-05 one wave away. The
  //   tag puts that claim in the file somebody would edit rather than in a config
  //   comment they would not read. GONE as of the phase-1 review fixes: the seam
  //   turned out to be a no-op in production (nothing calls getDb twice), so it
  //   is now `resetDbHandleForTest`, consumed by the specs like the other three
  //   reset seams, and needs no tag.
  //
  // Exports tagged `@internal` are excluded from reporting.
  //
  // This is what makes `ignoreExportsUsedInFile: false` liveable without either
  // deleting seams that are spoken for or reinstating a flag that hides a whole
  // class. The exemption moves from this file, which nobody reads while editing
  // code, into a JSDoc tag on the declaration itself — the same reasoning plan
  // 01-03 gave for the one `@public` tag it used, and `@internal` is a standard
  // TSDoc tag that means exactly what is being claimed: not part of this
  // package's public surface.
  //
  // A NEW dead export is still reported. Silencing one is a deliberate, visible,
  // reviewable edit at the declaration.
  "tags": ["-internal"],

  // FALSE as of plan 05-01, discharging the note above.
  //
  // The hole was opened in Phase 1 for a stated reason — sixteen types exported
  // but referenced only inside their own module — and left open with a stated
  // condition for closing it: "when the frontend in Phase 5 gives most of these
  // types a cross-module consumer". Phase 5 arrived, so the flag comes off
  // rather than becoming permanent by default, which is how a temporary
  // exemption normally ends its life.
  //
  // With it off, a genuinely dead export that happens to be referenced once in
  // its own file is reported again. Any export that still needs an exemption is
  // named INDIVIDUALLY below rather than the flag being reinstated wholesale:
  // a per-export exemption states which one and invites the question why; a
  // global flag hides the whole class and stops anyone asking.
  "ignoreExportsUsedInFile": false,
  "rules": {
    "exports": "error",
    "types": "error"
  }
}
